{
  "comment": "SDE theme palettes: the single source of the colors and shapes of every SDE theme family. tools/build-themes.py uses it for the GTK overlays, libadwaita colors and Openbox themes, and writes generated/theme_palettes.h for sde::Theme (src/common/theme.cpp). Colors are #RRGGBB; shadow_alpha, mica and translucency are 0-1. Since 0.2.0 Alpha 2 (the redesign) every family has its own character on one shared grammar: neutral surfaces in three steps (background, surface, surface_alt), hairline borders, text and dimmed text that keep WCAG AA (also the inactive title), soft corners in three sizes (radius_small for controls, radius for windows, menus and cards, radius_large for popups and big surfaces) and Mint-Y like caption buttons on the right (soft discs, a muted red close while hovered; caption sets the hit area in percent of the title height, the spacing in pixels and that red). SDE Graphite is calm and neutral, SDE Fluent a cool slate with Mica, SDE Liquid Glass luminous glass with the softest corners; its liquid block holds the material of the Liquid Glass compositor shader (see docs/THEMES.md).",
